            <ArticleTitle>Leriche's syndrome with total perfusion of the left lower extremity by way of the left internal mammary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>997-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of collateral perfusion of a lower extremity by way of an internal mammary artery in the presence of Leriche's syndrome is described. The importance of recognizing this condition before coronary artery bypass grafting is emphasized.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
